/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Today, Rajgad is one of the most revered and popular hill forts in the Pune district, attracting numerous trekkers and visitors annually who seek to explore its distinct layout of the Balekilla and three sub-plateaus \(Padmavati, Sanjeevani, and Suvela Machis\). This fort is a living monument to the Maratha golden age, with visible remains of temples, water cisterns \(Talai\), fortification walls, and the ruins of the Rajwada \(palace\), all of which deeply contribute to the regional identity and memory.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
