206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (Rajgad sits in the Mawal, a landscape of forested ridges, narrow valleys, and fast rivers whose terrain actively channelled any approaching army into prepared defensive positions. The Kanadi River, which must be crossed on both the Pali and Gunjavane approaches, becomes a genuine military obstacle during monsoon months. The nullahs dissecting the hillsides in every direction made rapid movement nearly impossible, while the forests provided cover for the Mavale warriors who knew every stream crossing and hidden path. The fort did not wait for attackers to reach its walls to begin its defence that defence began kilometres away, in the terrain itself.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
