/P 118 0 R
/E (A Natural Fortress in the Sahyadris)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (The Western Ghats were formed by the Deccan Traps eruption approximately 65 million years ago, producing the dense, layered basalt visible in every cliff face and fortress wall across Maharashtra. The Sahyadris drop sharply westward toward the Konkan coast and descend more gradually eastward toward the Deccan plateau an asymmetry that made western approaches nearly impassable for medieval armies. The basalt's natural jointing created sheer, vertical cliff faces that served as inherent defensive features; wherever nature left a gap, the builders filled it with their own stone. The distinction between the geological and the architectural is often invisible to the modern eye.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
