/E (Rajgad's defensive architecture is built around a central Balekilla and three fortified spurs or Machis, each functioning as an autonomous defensive unit. The Mughal chronicler Saqi Mustaid Khan described the three Machis as three separate forts built by Shivaji around the main structure, while the Sabhasad records four major defensive points including the Balekilla itself.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (The three Machis sit at comparable elevations well below the central citadel. Suvela Machi lies to the southeast at 1,183 metres, Sanjeevani Machi to the southwest at 1,185 metres, and Padmavati Machi at 1,195 metres. The Balekilla at 1,394 metres forms the fort's highest point.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
