332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 130 0 R
/T (As the sole eastern entry point to the fort complex, the Padmavati Machi controlled all movement between the lower approaches and the Balekilla above, making it the critical threshold of the entire defensive system. Its defences include strong fort walls and a parakota \(inner line of defence\). Much of the western fortification line has collapsed, leaving only foundations, upon which modern conservation work has added an ashlar masonry parapet. The western flanks feature bastions B1, B2, and B3, while bastion B35 to the east remains largely intact and provides a broad terrace for surveillance. Secret exits known as Chordarwazas were built into the defensive system to allow controlled movement during times of danger, one of which lies north of the Padmavati Talav.)
/E (As the sole eastern entry point to the fort complex, the Padmavati Machi controlled all movement between the lower approaches and the Balekilla above, making it the critical threshold of the entire defensive system. Its defences include strong fort walls and a parakota \(inner line of defence\). Much of the western fortification line has collapsed, leaving only foundations, upon which modern conservation work has added an ashlar masonry parapet. The western flanks feature bastions B1, B2, and B3, while bastion B35 to the east remains largely intact and provides a broad terrace for surveillance. Secret exits known as Chordarwazas were built into the defensive system to allow controlled movement during times of danger, one of which lies north of the Padmavati Talav.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
