<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 130 0 R
/T (Beyond its military role, the Padmavati Machi housed the royal court or sadar, granaries, and major military facilities, sustaining Rajgad's function as the Maratha capital.)
/E (Beyond its military role, the Padmavati Machi housed the royal court or sadar, granaries, and major military facilities, sustaining Rajgad's function as the Maratha capital.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 130 0 R
/T (The Padmavati Talav is a sacred oval-shaped freshwater lake situated north of the Padmavati Temple, with a depth of 30 feet and intact containment walls. An arched entryway built as a continuation of the lake wall marks its entrance, though the tank currently suffers from significant silting. The waters are notably white in colour during the monsoon and winter months.)
/E (The Padmavati Talav is a sacred oval-shaped freshwater lake situated north of the Padmavati Temple, with a depth of 30 feet and intact containment walls. An arched entryway built as a continuation of the lake wall marks its entrance, though the tank currently suffers from significant silting. The waters are notably white in colour during the monsoon and winter months.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 130 0 R
/T (Local tradition holds that before Navaratri, the lake would dry up to reveal the divine ornaments and utensils of Padmavati Devi for use in the festival's rituals. This sacred tradition was broken when a devotee removed one of the utensils, after which the ornaments never reappeared, an event locals interpret as the Devi's curse.)
/E (Local tradition holds that before Navaratri, the lake would dry up to reveal the divine ornaments and utensils of Padmavati Devi for use in the festival's rituals. This sacred tradition was broken when a devotee removed one of the utensils, after which the ornaments never reappeared, an event locals interpret as the Devi's curse.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
