/E (Stretching approximately 2 kilometres along the southwestern ridge, Sanjeevani Machi is among the finest examples of Maratha defensive architecture in the entire Deccan. Nineteen bastions run along its length in a triple-segmented construction, nine reinforced with inner chilkhati buruj. The westernmost, Bastion B13, integrates natural rock with structural masonry to rise 37.28 metres the height of a twelve-storey building, built on the edge of a cliff, without machinery. A subterranean passage within Bastion B8 provided shelter from bombardment and the capacity for surprise counterattack, making the defence here not merely vertical but three-dimensional.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
