/P 132 0 R
/E (Extending southeast toward the rising sun its name meaning the auspicious time, reflecting this eastward orientation Suvela Machi is narrow, elongated, and primarily military in character. Its seventeen bastions, seven of them chilkhati buruj, guard a ridge that commands the eastern approaches. The most dramatic natural feature on the entire fort is here: the Hatti Prastar, a rock formation resembling a colossal east-facing elephant, atop which stands the Tehalni Buruj, the Watch Bastion. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
