/P 132 0 R
/E (Whether the Rameshwar Temple and nearby structures date from Shivaji Maharaj's reign or predate it remains uncertain. Historical records suggest that around 1490 CE, Ahmed Bahiri, founder of the Nizam Shahi dynasty, captured Murumdev and destroyed many of its temples, and the current ruins may reflect damage from this period. The remaining ruined structures likely served as barracks or support facilities, completing the Machi's combination of defensive, residential, and logistical functions.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [8]
>>
