373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The bhuyari parakota the subterranean defensive passage found in the third tier of Bastion B8 \(the Vyaghra Buruj\) on Sanjeevani Machi adds a dimension to the fort's defence that attackers could never anticipate. Connected to the outer wall by hidden steps, this underground passage provided both shelter from bombardment and the capacity for surprise sorties. Attackers fighting through the outer tiers could not know that below their feet, defenders were moving unseen toward positions from which a counterattack could be launched. The architecture of Rajgad's defence was not merely vertical it was fully three-dimensional, built into the rock itself.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
