375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The Pali Darwaza is the primary entry to Rajgad the Rajmarg, the King's Road, deliberately built wide enough for elephants bearing howdahs. The approach from Velhe, crossing the Kanadi River and climbing the Khariw Ghat, reaches a rock-cut ascent in short zigzags engineered for the passage of large animals and ceremonial processions. At the summit, the Mukhya Darwaza presents ashlar bastions with merlons and arrowslits, rounded phalikas designed for small cannons, a surveillance window, and arcaded guardrooms, monitoring all movement. Above the arch, a carved royal crown announces in stone whose fort this was and under whose authority every visitor entered.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
