/Title (The front portico near the entrance is known as the talghar, while the larger hall behind it likely served as the main administrative and congregational chamber. Also present along the western bastion are the heavily ruined remains of the Rajwada \(royal residence\) and the Kacheri \(administrative assembly hall\), of which only foundation courses survive. East of the Padmavati Talav, a long rectangular row of uniform square cells arranged along a north-south axis may have served as a commercial or storage facility supporting the fort's logistical needs.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
