/Title (South of the temple complex along the paved pathway lies the Darukothar, the former gunpowder magazine of the Padmavati Machi. This small west-facing structure of plain ashlar masonry stands on a paved plinth, with a single western entrance and a bare, undivided interior hall.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1316 0 R
/Next 1305 0 R
>>
endobj
1311 0 obj
<<
/Title (Rajgad Fort is as remarkable for its architecture as it is for its history. Perched on a central cone rising to approximately 1,376 metres \(4,514 ft\), the fort showcases a sophisticated multi-tiered design that integrates military construction with its dramatic Sahyadri terrain. Its layout is divided into four interconnected sections, the central Balekilla \(citadel\) and three expansive sub-plateaus or Machis, giving it a distinctive tricorn shape with a total circumference of around 40 kilometres.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1307 0 R
/First 1317 0 R
/Last 1317 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
